   "A piece partway through an extreme verdict word or phrase, good or bad, before the rest of it arrives: inner chunks of a long or ALL-CAPS intense adjective or adverb split into several tokens (INC-RED-IBLE, F-ANT-ASTIC, HORR-IBLE, extra-ordinary, зам-еч-ательный, ч-рез-вычайно) and the opening words of a superlative idiom after a praising lead-in (state- of the art, world-class, show-stopping, out of this world). Quiet on intense words that arrive as one whole token (amazing, incredible, breathtaking), on mild verdicts (mediocre, pretty good), and on the same opening words used literally (the top of the hill, around the world).",
